# A Kannada conjunct that UAX #29 cuts into several clusters takes the
# cells of each cluster (ADR-1006 D2). Kannada's virama has no
# Indic_Conjunct_Break=Linker, so stree is three clusters: sa with the
# virama, ta with the virama, and ra with the vowel sign ii. They take 1, 1
# and 2 cells, 4 in all, as glibc's wcswidth counts the word. Kra is ka
# with the virama and then ra, two clusters of one cell each.
# spec: UAX #29 GB9c; Python wcwidth 0.9.4's specification, "Scope": "Each string yielded by wcwidth.iter_graphemes may be mapped to wcwidth.wcswidth to accurately measure the width of a grapheme"; ADR-1006 D2
# covers: text.grapheme
size 10 2
send "\u{CB8}\u{CCD}\u{CA4}\u{CCD}\u{CB0}\u{CC0}"
dump state
send "\u{C95}\u{CCD}\u{CB0}"
dump state
